OSP JWT Token Validator
Open Service Platform

!!! Introduction

The <*poco.jwt*> bundle registers the service <[osp.jwt.validator]>, a
Poco::OSP::Web::TokenValidator for JSON Web Tokens (JWTs). The web server uses
it for bearer token authentication if <[osp.web.tokenValidatorName]> is set to
<[osp.jwt.validator]>.

A token is accepted if all of the following hold:

  - It is signed with one of the configured algorithms and the configured key
    of that algorithm.
  - Its expiration time (claim "exp") has not passed by more than the leeway.
    A token without an expiration time is rejected.
  - Its "not before" time (claim "nbf"), if it has one, is not later than the
    leeway from now.
  - It names a subject (claim "sub").
  - It names the configured issuer (claim "iss") and the configured audience
    (claim "aud"), if they are configured.

The subject is the name of the user, and the claim "scope", if the token has
one, is the scope of the request.

NOTE: Without jwt.validator.issuer, the issuer of a token is not checked, and
without jwt.validator.audience, its audience is not checked: a token that the
configured key signed for another service is accepted if it meets the other
conditions. Set both if the key also signs tokens for other services.


!!! Configuring the Bundle

The bundle is configured using the global application configuration file.
The following configuration properties are available:


!! jwt.validator.algorithms

The algorithms that a token may be signed with, separated by commas or
semicolons. Default is HS256. The supported algorithms are HS256, HS384,
HS512, RS256, RS384, RS512, ES256, ES384 and ES512. An algorithm that is not
supported, or for which no key is configured, is logged as a warning when the
bundle starts; tokens signed with it are rejected.


!! jwt.validator.hmac.key

The secret key for the algorithms HS256, HS384 and HS512. Default is empty.


!! jwt.validator.rsa.publicKey

The public key for the algorithms RS256, RS384 and RS512, in PEM format (the
text of the key, not a file name). Default is empty.


!! jwt.validator.ec.publicKey

The public key for the algorithms ES256, ES384 and ES512, in PEM format (the
text of the key, not a file name). Default is empty.


!! jwt.validator.leeway

The time in seconds by which the expiration time may have passed and the
"not before" time may lie in the future, to allow for differences between the
clocks of the issuer and of this process. Default is 5.


!! jwt.validator.issuer

The issuer that a token must name. Default is empty: the issuer is not checked.


!! jwt.validator.audience

The audience that a token must name, as its only audience or as one of
several. Default is empty: the audience is not checked.
